meta {
  name: 03 - Rejected (Multiple Hard Rule Violations)
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/loan/prequalify
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "description": "My income is $3000 a month and I have $2000 in monthly debt payments already. I've been at my current job for about a year. I want to borrow $300,000. My credit score is around 500."
  }
}

docs {
  Should trigger THREE separate hard-rule failures simultaneously: credit
  score below minimum, debt-to-income ratio too high, and loan-to-income
  ratio too high. All three should appear in decision.reasons together,
  not just the first one encountered.

  defaultProbability and riskBand should both be null in the response,
  proving the rules engine short-circuited BEFORE the gRPC call to the
  Python risk scorer ever happened. If you added the print() logging line
  to server.py's ScoreLoan method, confirm nothing gets printed there for
  this request.
}
